<title>BRAZIL: Brazil posts net dlr inflows of $1.35 bln in April.</title>
<headline>Brazil posts net dlr inflows of $1.35 bln in April.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange transactions showed a preliminary surplus of $1.35 billion in April in the forex commercial market, against a revised $1.173 billion surplus in March, bankers said.</p>
<p>Financial buy deals totalled $6.891 billion in April, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.  Financial sell operations amounted to $5.427 billion last month.</p>
<p>Dealers said April contracted exports were $5.054 billion, and import operations totalled $5.168 billion.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5418))</p>
